  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-20--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2022-tame-20: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.38" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.375"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "A controlled reinforcement-learning assay could clearly test the prediction. The required training histories and morphological readouts are not available in existing public datasets, so new experiments are necessary." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Repeatedly pair tissue states or actions with prespecified rewards or punishments, then test on held-out conditions whether morphology or expression shifts toward a rewarded target more than yoked and unpaired controls." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The paper explicitly describes the prediction as untested.", "Public datasets do not appear to contain reinforcement schedules with longitudinal anatomical outcomes.", "Distinguishing learning from selection or toxicity requires new controls." .
